# =====================================================================
# Release V116 -- Open-plans exclusions + Recall fk_Practitioner
# =====================================================================
# 1) Open Courses must NOT count zero-value or inactive-patient plans as open. Fact_Treatment_Plans
#    Course_Status now reclassifies a would-be-open plan to 'Closed - Excluded' when it has no
#    outstanding private value OR the patient is inactive -- so every Open Courses measure + report
#    (which filter Course_Status IN 'In Progress'/'Open - No Appointment') drops them automatically.
# 2) Fact_Recalls gains fk_Practitioner = the patient's DENTIST or HYGIENIST (chosen by recall type),
#    so recalls drill/filter by practitioner like the other facts. Table is DROP/CREATE -> reload
#    populates it fresh. NOTE: still needs the MODEL relationship _Recalls.fk Practitioner ->
#    List Practitioners (add via Tabular Editor/Desktop) for the drill-through to bite.
#
# APPLY: after deploy, Orchestrate_Build reloads Fact_Treatment_Plans (hash-updates the reclassified
# Course_Status) + repopulates Fact_Recalls, and regenerates the PBI views (fk_Practitioner surfaces).
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V116__open_plans_exclusions_recall_practitioner.manifest -SkipTests
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY   Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Fact_Treatment_Plans.StoredProcedure.sql
DEPLOY   Fabric\Gold.Fact_Recalls.Table.sql
DEPLOY   Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Fact_Recalls.StoredProcedure.sql
EXEC     EXEC Meta.usp_Create_Gold_Views;

TEST
